Description: Restore the public session save/restore API of GtkApplication.
 GTK 4.21.0 added state saving to GtkApplication: an application which sets GtkApplication:support-save has GTK
 save the state of its windows, including the name under which the compositor remembers where each window was
 placed, and restore it at the next start with GtkApplication::restore-window. The public API was removed before
 4.22 (merge request 9395, commit 031658a006), which left the machinery in place without a way to turn it on.
 This is upstream's own revert of that removal, cherry-picked unchanged. It was applied on main after 4.22 had
 branched, and the API was hidden again for 4.24 (merge request 10196, commit eabaa008d5) because its
 replacement, which lets applications save and restore asynchronously, did not land in time.
Author: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/commit/15ed5c2fea8ff8568110d5b86c148c02968166e4
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/merge_requests/9623
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
